# Build context is the repo root (see infra/docker/compose.yaml), so this file
# has to live here rather than beside the Dockerfile.
#
# The Dockerfile only COPYs bus/, router/ and db/, so this is the second guard
# rather than the only one. It matters anyway: without it the daemon uploads
# the whole tree as build context first, including voice/whisper/ (a multi-GB
# build tree with the model and the FlexML runtime in it) and Ali's wake-word
# recordings. That is minutes of upload and personal audio crossing a boundary
# it has no business crossing, on every build.

.git/
.gitignore
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.pytest-basetemp/
.pytest-typing-diagnosis/

# Secrets and local state. None of this may ever enter an image layer.
.env
*.db
*.db-*
*.seen-messages.db
*.mem0-history.db
.executor-heartbeat

# Executor-side and laptop-only. Nothing the bus/router/db/memory image
# copies lives here.
voice/
ingest/
tools/
tests/
docs/
infra/terraform/
scripts/

# executor/ and memory/ are no longer blanket-excluded: bus-offbox-packaging
# (9 Sep 2026) made the Dockerfile COPY memory/ in full (recall/remember run
# in the bus process now) and a named handful of executor/ modules
# (conversation/, handlers/command_intent.py, handlers/outcome.py,
# handlers/whatsapp.py, latency.py, notify.py, __init__.py) -- an ignored
# parent directory here would make those COPY lines fail outright, since the
# daemon never receives an ignored path as build context at all. What stays
# excluded is what the Dockerfile never names and never should: the modules
# with a heavy or platform-specific import surface, kept out even though the
# Dockerfile's own selective COPY already would not touch them, because two
# guards catch what one guard misses.
executor/flp/
executor/system_control/
executor/app_automation/
executor/heartbeat.py
executor/poller.py
executor/handlers/distill.py

# Build artifacts and logs
*.log
*.zip
node_modules/
